Negative control for the area's panels being bootable by the harness (RT1).

The registry flattens an area into one binding per panel, keyed
`<area>.<panel>`, and the harness builds a boot thunk for every key that binds a
composable. Without a thunk a replay step cannot boot the panel's cell and
`World.boot("affiliate.links", …)` fails at the key. This mutant builds thunks
for the single-surface scenarios only, so every panel of every area is
unbootable while the pages still draw.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (module lane): self-drawn-binding.spec.ts — every panel key of an
area must be present in the harness registry as a function, and an area's own
key must not be.

